# Design System Rule for Migraine Tracker App

description: >
  UI/UX rule for the Migraine Tracker App built with Next.js and the ixartz SaaS Boilerplate. 
  Defines visual style, component usage, design tokens, and layout behavior for consistent design.
  Target users are migraine sufferers. Prioritize clean, calm, mobile-first interfaces.

stack:
  - Next.js
  - Tailwind CSS
  - shadcn/ui
  - Heroicons or Lucide icons
  - Chart.js or Recharts (for data viz)

visual-style:
  theme: light with soft, calming tone
  accentColor: '#6B7CFF'  # Gentle blue, used for buttons, highlights, etc.
  background: '#FFFFFF'
  surface: '#F9FAFB'
  textColor: '#1F2937'     # Dark gray
  borderRadius: '0.75rem'  # Rounded-xl
  spacingScale: Tailwind default (0.5rem steps)

components:
  buttons:
    primary: filled, rounded, accent background, white text
    secondary: outline, gray border, dark text
    state: hover/active/focus styles required
  forms:
    inputs: rounded-md, light background, border
    datePicker: use shadcn/ui
    select: use shadcn/ui
    validation: red text + border for error
  dialogs:
    use shadcn/ui Dialog or Drawer for multi-step flows
  icons:
    use Heroicons (outline) or Lucide with consistent stroke width
  charts:
    use Chart.js or Recharts; match accent color; minimalist axis/grid

typography:
  font: system-ui or Inter
  sizes:
    base: 16px
    heading: 20–28px
    helperText: 14px
  hierarchy: use Tailwind font weights and spacing for clarity

layout:
  responsive: mobile-first
  nav: bottom navigation on mobile; sidebar or topbar on desktop
  cards: use soft shadows, spacing, rounded corners
  forms: multi-step logging (optional), inline guidance where helpful

accessibility:
  contrast: WCAG AA compliant
  darkMode: planned, not default
  animations: gentle fade/slide only; no flashing
  touchTargets: min 40px tap size

community:
  layout: list of posts with preview text
  actions: post, comment, react (like/heart)
  moderation: not included in MVP

output-guidelines:
  - Always use Tailwind + shadcn components
  - No inline styles or external UI libraries
  - Use consistent spacing and accent colors
  - All UI should be accessible and responsive by default
